  "notes": "The research calls him \"Griselda's most song-shaped member\", and two parameters are what that means here. First, hats: he is the only entry in this Buffalo cluster with `hihat.continuous` true, at `fillDensity` 0.44 — the research says \"some 8th hats (more than his labelmates)\" — while Westside Gunn, Conway, Boldy James and Mach-Hommy all run a non-continuous stream at the 0.28–0.32 floor. Second, hooks: `chords` is a real progression set rather than `impliedByRiff`, because the research says his loops carry \"slightly more motion — i–iv, i–VI–VII\", and `sectionRules.hook` is a full 8-bar section with the countermelody added, because he has \"actual 8-bar hooks\" where his labelmates have none. Light swing is 0.56, between the archetype's 0.58 and Conway's near-straight 0.52; the kit stays dry and un-reverbed, so `velocityTiers` sits below the archetype's ceiling but well above Westside Gunn's. ⚠ `confidence` is medium and the research marks artist-level specifics `[LOW-CONF]` — the label idiom is documented, this member's session is not. ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameter to name is `bassline.glideProb` 0.18: the research says \"on the major-label material a modern 808 with short glide appears\" without saying how often, and 0.18 is this author's reading of \"appears\" rather than \"is the sound\". The velocity tiers and hat densities are the same kind of inference.",
